      "title": "Snider half-cocking rifle",
      "audio": "audio/en/AB003.mp3",
      "sections": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "content": "Single barrel. This weapon's original design was the work of Jacob Snider of New York. The British Government accepted the design to the ends of transforming their Enfield muzzleloaders into breechloaders. The military counterpart to this gun was Britain's first rifle which in 1869 fired metal rounds."
        },
